"Runic Enchanting": {
  "index": -2,
  "category": "enchantments",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Runic Enchanting"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "The first step in runic enchanting is to "
        },
        {
          "text": "scribe and forge a rune",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " according to the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runescribing",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runeforging",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " mechanics. The enchantment's recipe will let me know which one(s) I need to make.\n\nI remember seeing information elsewhere in this book about "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runescribing, Runeforging",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and how to do them both.\n\nOnce I have my rune made, I will need to infuse mana into it to apply the initial stage of the enchantment to the rune.\n\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Place the rune along with any other required reagents from the recipe into a",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "Manaweaving Altar",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Then, using a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Manaweaver's Wand",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "I'll draw or project the required patterns from the recipe on top of the altar",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". If I've done it correctly, the altar should draw in the manaweaves and items to create an "
        },
        {
          "text": "enchanted rune",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nAll that's left now is to "
        },
        {
          "text": "combine the rune with an item back at the runic anvil",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nI'll need to place the "
        },
        {
          "text": "item I want to enchant",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runic Anvil",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " and the "
        },
        {
          "text": "enchanted rune",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " on top. \n\nIf the enchantment can be applied to the item "
        },
        {
          "text": "(standard combination and compatibility rules apply)",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "I will see the magic of the anvil activate",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nThen, to finish the enchant, I need to "
        },
        {
          "text": "strike the rune with a Runesmith's Hammer repeatedly until the enchantment is applied",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  If the anvil's magic is not active when I hit it with the hammer, the items will be ejected.\n\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "The enchantments you can make are determined by your tier. Should you obtain an enchantment on a rune that doesn't have a matching recipe (for example on a ",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Projection Rune",
          "italic": true,
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " using the ",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Disenchanter",
          "italic": true,
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "), the freeform enchanting rules are used:",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": "\n\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "- Enchantment levels 1-2 require you to be Tier 3",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "- Enchantment levels 3-4 require you to be Tier 4",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "- Enchantment levels 5+ require you to be Tier 5",
          "italic": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
